Aim
To write a Python program using Matplotlib to create and display different types of graphs, such as bar chart, line chart, pie chart, scatter plot and histogram, for visualizing subject marks.

Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Matplotlib library.
3. Create lists containing subject names and their marks.
4. Create a bar chart using plt.bar().
5. Add a title and axis labels, and display the bar chart.
6. Create a line chart using plt.plot().
7. Add a title and axis labels, and display the line chart.
8. Create a pie chart using plt.pie().
9. Display the pie chart with percentage labels.
10. Create a scatter plot using plt.scatter().
11. Add a title and axis labels, and display the scatter plot.
12. Create a histogram using plt.hist().
13. Add a title and axis labels, and display the histogram.
14. Stop the program.

code

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Data
subjects = ["Python", "Java", "DBMS", "OS"]
marks = [90, 80, 85, 95]

# 1. Bar Chart
plt.figure()
plt.bar(subjects, marks)
plt.title("Bar Chart")
plt.xlabel("Subjects")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.show()

# 2. Line Chart
plt.figure()
plt.plot(subjects, marks, marker='o')
plt.title("Line Chart")
plt.xlabel("Subjects")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.show()

# 3. Pie Chart
plt.figure()
plt.pie(marks, labels=subjects, autopct='%1.1f%%')
plt.title("Pie Chart")
plt.show()

# 4. Scatter Plot
plt.figure()
plt.scatter(subjects, marks)
plt.title("Scatter Plot")
plt.xlabel("Subjects")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.show()

# 5. Histogram
plt.figure()
plt.hist(marks, bins=4)
plt.title("Histogram")
plt.xlabel("Marks")
plt.ylabel("Frequency")
plt.show()

